        "original_id": "a94a7f24-1ef5-5149-9526-7a15cbadc6a2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chris Kraft, Gene Kranz, Jim Lovell, Jerry Bostick, Ed Fendell, Gene Cernan, John Llewellen, John Aaron, Glynn Lunney, Wally Schirra, Gerry Griffin, Ed Harris\n- Works: Failure Is Not an Option, Apollo 13\n- Organizations: NASA\n- Roles: Flight Director\n- Programs: Gemini, Apollo, Apollo 11, Apollo 13\n\nFacts:\n- Failure Is Not an Option was produced in 2003.\n- Failure Is Not an Option included speakers Chris Kraft, Gene Kranz, Jim Lovell, Jerry Bostick, Ed Fendell, Gene Cernan, John Llewellen, John Aaron, Glynn Lunney, Wally Schirra, and Gerry Griffin.\n- Gene Kranz served as a NASA Flight Director during the Gemini and Apollo programs.\n- Gene Kranz succeeded NASA founding Flight Director Chris Kraft.\n- Gene Kranz served as flight director during Apollo 11, the first lunar landing.\n- Gene Kranz is best known for directing the Mission Control team efforts that saved the crew of Apollo 13.\n- Apollo 13 later became the subject of a major motion picture of the same name in which Ed Harris portrayed Gene Kranz.",
